@startuml
' Evidence: Laplace-UCI/src/Laplace.Uci/Program.cs SHA256 c75d540aac8af80dcdb95b020a41680eba2587cec64b2e48a260a6a091681072
' Evidence: Laplace-UCI/src/Laplace.Uci/Connections.cs SHA256 804a8785d1e69fd88ab4d3e519c50754ad2408b1767a2c3b12975bb32d30cbd4
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title UCI connector — engine verification probe
start

:Open configured engine;
:Start 120-second lifetime deadline;
:Send uci; receive until uciok;
:Send isready; receive until readyok;
:Send ucinewgame; send isready; receive until readyok;
:Send position startpos; send go depth 1;
:Receive until bestmove;
if (Last retained line exactly bestmove 0000 or bestmove (none)?) then (yes)
 :Throw no-move error;
else (no)
 :Print profile metadata, UTC time and retained protocol lines;
endif
:Dispose engine;
legend
Until reports info-string diagnostics to stderr and retains at most 256 selected lines.
Selected lines include engine ID, best move, providers, database identity and knowledge identity.
EOF before expected response throws; timeout cancels the shared lifetime token.
The outer command catch prints errors and returns 1.
endlegend
stop
footer
Source-reviewed orchestration. Nested semantics remain open; no runtime acceptance
claimed. The timeout starts after connection opening. This is a handshake and minimal
response probe: the wrapper does not independently validate move legality, chess strength
or declared knowledge content. Null-move rejection is an exact string comparison. No
engine process or connector endpoint was started.
end footer

@enduml
